---
import ResourceLayout from '../../layouts/ResourceLayout.astro';
import { resources, resourceUrl } from '../../data/resources';
const names = ['MTTD and response-time calculator', 'Editable incident response plan', 'Tabletop exercise scenarios'];
---
<ResourceLayout title="Free incident response resources and exercises" description="Explore a response-time calculator, an editable incident response plan and tabletop scenarios. Free resources from the Confronto Cibernético book site." path="/en/incident-response-resources/" english>
  <header class="resource-hero"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN · PRACTISE · SHARE</p><h1>Incident response<br><em>in practice.</em></h1><p>Practical resources for exploring evidence, coordination and recovery decisions. The calculator is available in English and Portuguese. The book, plan generator and tabletop exercises are in Portuguese; this guide explains their purpose in English.</p><div class="resource-badges"><span>Free access</span><span>No registration</span><span>Inputs processed in your browser</span></div><a href="/recursos/" hreflang="pt-BR">Leia em português ↗</a></header>
  <section class="resource-grid" aria-label="Available resources">{resources.map((resource,index)=><article><p class="eyebrow">RESOURCE {index+1}</p><h2>{names[index]}</h2><p>{index===0 ? 'Calculate mean, median and nearest-rank P90 for detection, containment and recovery durations. The example data is fictional, and the tool makes its time boundaries explicit.' : index===1 ? 'Generate a Markdown working draft covering scope, roles, escalation, evidence, communication and recovery. Adapt and approve it with the responsible people in your organisation.' : 'Discuss fictional ransomware, cloud-account and persistence scenarios in five rounds. Export a worksheet to record decisions, evidence gaps and improvement actions.'}</p><a class="text-link" href={index===0 ? '/en/mttd-mttr-calculator/' : resourceUrl(resource)}>{index===0 ? 'Open calculator in English' : 'Open resource in Portuguese'} ↗</a></article>)}</section>
  <section class="resource-explainer"><h2>Use the resources to make a decision reviewable</h2><p>Start with one question that matters to your team. For a measurement exercise, identify the event that starts each clock and the condition that stops it. For a plan, identify who can approve a disruptive containment action. For a tabletop discussion, record what was known when the decision was made and what would cause you to reconsider it.</p><p>The calculator uses one incident per row, with three durations in minutes separated by semicolons: initial activity to detection; detection to containment; detection to recovery. It reports the last interval explicitly rather than assuming that every organisation uses MTTR with the same meaning. Small samples and uncertain start times require careful interpretation.</p><p>The plan generator produces a working draft, not an assessment of readiness. The tabletop scenarios are fictional conversations and do not execute attacks or test your infrastructure. A useful outcome is a specific improvement with an owner and a way to verify completion.</p><h2>About the book</h2><p><em>Confronto Cibernético</em>, by Hiago Kin Levi and published by Brasport, discusses advanced persistent threats, incident response and coordination between defensive operations and threat intelligence. The edition described on this website is in Portuguese. <a href="/autor/en/">Read the author biography in English</a> or <a href="/#comprar">view the available editions</a>.</p><h2>Further study</h2><p>For current external guidance, consult <a href="https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/61/r3/final">NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 3</a> and the <a href="https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/cybersecurity-scenarios">CISA cybersecurity scenarios</a>. These are independent references; the resources on this website are not endorsed or certified by those organisations.</p><p>You can link students and colleagues directly to any resource. The downloaded plan and exercise worksheets include permission for adaptation in internal or educational activities with attribution. The book, its cover and third-party material retain their own rights.</p><p>Follow updates through the <a href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a> or suggest an improvement using the <a href="/imprensa/#contato">contact form</a>.</p></section>
</ResourceLayout>
